# Runtime application data must never enter the image either. The container
# gets its database from the SQLITE_DATA_DIR bind mount at /app/data, never from
# the build context: a copied portal.db would bake real member records into a
# published image. sqlite/schema.sql and public/ are source and stay.
#
# Docker's bare `*.sqlite` matches the context root only, so every extension is
# written both ways: `**/` covers a nested `nested/path/sample.sqlite`. Keep this
# list in step with .gitignore and scripts/check-no-runtime-data.sh.
#
# Store directories are named by suffix, not `**/data`, because Docker's `**/`
# also matches zero directories and would drop `src/lib/data/` and `public/data/`.
